  ('algorithms', 3, 'What is Binary Search?', 'Beginner', '**
Binary Search finds a target value within a **sorted** array. It compares the target value to the middle element of the array. If they are unequal, the half in which the target cannot lie is eliminated. Complexity: O(log n).', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
**
Binary Search finds a target value within a **sorted** array. It compares the target value to the middle element of the array. If they are unequal, the half in which the target cannot lie is eliminated. Complexity: O(log n).

**Code Example**:
```javascript
function binarySearch(arr, target) {
  let l = 0,
    r = arr.length - 1;
  while (l <= r) {
    const mid = Math.floor((l + r) / 2);
    if (arr[mid] === target) return mid;
    if (arr[mid] < target) l = mid + 1;
    else r = mid - 1;
  }
  return -1;
}
```

