  ('algorithms', 15, 'Explain Dijkstra''s Algorithm?', 'Advanced', '**
Finds shortest paths from a source to all other nodes in a weighted graph. Use a **Priority Queue** (Min-Heap). Greedily select the node with the smallest known distance and update neighbors.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
**
Finds shortest paths from a source to all other nodes in a weighted graph. Use a **Priority Queue** (Min-Heap). Greedily select the node with the smallest known distance and update neighbors.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
// Conceptual
function dijkstra(graph, start) {
  const dist = {}; // Init with Infinity
  const pq = new MinHeap();
  pq.push(0, start);

  while (!pq.isEmpty()) {
    const [d, u] = pq.pop();
    if (d > dist[u]) continue;
    for (let [v, weight] of graph[u]) {
      if (dist[u] + weight < dist[v]) {
        dist[v] = dist[u] + weight;
        pq.push(dist[v], v);
      }
    }
  }
}
```

