  ('algorithms', 19, 'Longest Increasing Subsequence (LIS)?', 'Advanced', '**
`dp[i]` = length of LIS ending at index `i`. Check all `j < i`, if `nums[i] > nums[j]`, update `dp[i]`. Time: O(n^2). Can be optimized to O(n log n) using Binary Search.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
**
`dp[i]` = length of LIS ending at index `i`. Check all `j < i`, if `nums[i] > nums[j]`, update `dp[i]`. Time: O(n^2). Can be optimized to O(n log n) using Binary Search.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
function lengthOfLIS(nums) {
  const dp = new Array(nums.length).fill(1);
  let max = 1;
  for (let i = 1; i < nums.length; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
      if (nums[i] > nums[j]) dp[i] = Math.max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1);
    }
    max = Math.max(max, dp[i]);
  }
  return max;
}
```

