  ('algorithms', 22, 'Implement Queue using Stacks?', 'Beginner', '**
Use two stacks: `input` and `output`. Push to `input`. Pop/Peek from `output`. If `output` empty, move all elements from `input` to `output` (reverses order).', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
**
Use two stacks: `input` and `output`. Push to `input`. Pop/Peek from `output`. If `output` empty, move all elements from `input` to `output` (reverses order).

**Code Example**:
```javascript
class MyQueue {
  constructor() {
    this.in = [];
    this.out = [];
  }
  push(x) {
    this.in.push(x);
  }
  pop() {
    if (!this.out.length) while (this.in.length) this.out.push(this.in.pop());
    return this.out.pop();
  }
}
```

