  ('algorithms', 25, 'Explain Trie (Prefix Tree)?', 'Advanced', '**
Tree structure for strings. Each node represents a character. Good for autocomplete, spell checker. Operations (Insert, Search, StartsWith) are O(L) where L is word length.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
**
Tree structure for strings. Each node represents a character. Good for autocomplete, spell checker. Operations (Insert, Search, StartsWith) are O(L) where L is word length.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = {};
    this.isEnd = false;
  }
}

class Trie {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
  }
  insert(word) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (let c of word) {
      if (!node.children[c]) node.children[c] = new TrieNode();
      node = node.children[c];
    }
    node.isEnd = true;
  }
}
```

