  ('algorithms', 28, 'Level Order Traversal (Tree)?', 'Intermediate', '**
Use BFS with a Queue. Process nodes level by level. Keep track of queue length at start of loop to process one level at a time.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
**
Use BFS with a Queue. Process nodes level by level. Keep track of queue length at start of loop to process one level at a time.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
function levelOrder(root) {
  if (!root) return [];
  const res = [],
    queue = [root];
  while (queue.length) {
    const level = [],
      len = queue.length;
    for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) {
      const node = queue.shift();
      level.push(node.val);
      if (node.left) queue.push(node.left);
      if (node.right) queue.push(node.right);
    }
    res.push(level);
  }
  return res;
}
```

