  ('aws', 45, 'Explain the SNS fan-out pattern with filter policies?', 'Intermediate', 'One SNS topic receives an event; many SQS queues subscribe so each downstream team gets its own copy with independent buffering, retries, and DLQs - producers stay decoupled from consumers. **Filter policies** on each subscription restrict delivery (attribute equality, `anything-but`, numeric ranges, exists) so a payments queue only receives `eventType=PAYMENT_CAPTURED` and SNS stops storing/sending irrelevant messages. Enable **raw message delivery** to cut cost and simplify parsing, use FIFO topics + FIFO queues when end-to-end ordering matters, and set subscription redrive policies for poison deliveries.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
One SNS topic receives an event; many SQS queues subscribe so each downstream team gets its own copy with independent buffering, retries, and DLQs - producers stay decoupled from consumers. **Filter policies** on each subscription restrict delivery (attribute equality, `anything-but`, numeric ranges, exists) so a payments queue only receives `eventType=PAYMENT_CAPTURED` and SNS stops storing/sending irrelevant messages. Enable **raw message delivery** to cut cost and simplify parsing, use FIFO topics + FIFO queues when end-to-end ordering matters, and set subscription redrive policies for poison deliveries.

**Code Example**:
```json
{
  "eventType": ["PAYMENT_CAPTURED", "PAYMENT_FAILED"],
  "amount": {"numeric": [">", 10000]},
  "currency": ["USD", "EUR"]
}
```

