  ('css', 24, 'How do you style a scrollbar using `::-webkit-scrollbar`?', 'Intermediate', 'Custom scrollbars improve visual consistency but come with a critical caveat: `::-webkit-scrollbar` only works in Chromium and Safari browsers. For Firefox, use the `scrollbar-width` and `scrollbar-color` standard properties. In production, consider whether custom scrollbars are necessary at all, as users may rely on the OS-level scrollbar for usability. Always test with both light and dark themes since scrollbars overlay the content.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

