  ('css', 25, 'How do you use `scroll-behavior: smooth`?', 'Intermediate', '`scroll-behavior: smooth` is the simplest way to add smooth scrolling for in-page anchor navigation, replacing JavaScript `scrollIntoView()` calls. Apply it to the `html` element for global behavior or to specific scroll containers. Pair it with `prefers-reduced-motion` to disable smooth scrolling for users who experience motion sensitivity, as abrupt stops during smooth scrolling can cause discomfort.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

