  ('css', 44, 'How do you pause an animation on hover?', 'Intermediate', '`animation-play-state` gives you control over running CSS animations without JavaScript, enabling interactive pause/resume behavior purely through CSS. This is useful for carousels, loading indicators, or any continuously animated element that should freeze on user interaction. A best practice is to always provide a clear visual cue (like reduced opacity) so users know the animation is intentionally paused.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
`animation-play-state` gives you control over running CSS animations without JavaScript, enabling interactive pause/resume behavior purely through CSS. This is useful for carousels, loading indicators, or any continuously animated element that should freeze on user interaction. A best practice is to always provide a clear visual cue (like reduced opacity) so users know the animation is intentionally paused.

```

