<a id="q53"></a>', NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
  ('css', 53, 'How do you style selection color (`::selection`)?', 'Intermediate', '`::selection` lets you customize the highlight appearance when users select text, reinforcing brand identity in a subtle but noticeable way. Only a limited set of properties work -- `color`, `background`, `text-shadow`, and `outline` -- so keep expectations realistic. A best practice is to ensure the selection colors maintain sufficient contrast for readability, as inverted colors can sometimes confuse users.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
`::selection` lets you customize the highlight appearance when users select text, reinforcing brand identity in a subtle but noticeable way. Only a limited set of properties work -- `color`, `background`, `text-shadow`, and `outline` -- so keep expectations realistic. A best practice is to ensure the selection colors maintain sufficient contrast for readability, as inverted colors can sometimes confuse users.

**Code Example**:
```css
::selection {
  background: gold;
  color: black;
}
```

