  ('design-patterns', 6, 'How do you use the Adapter Pattern to make incompatible interfaces work together?', 'Intermediate', '**
Wrap an existing class with a new interface so that it becomes compatible with the client''s expectations.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
**
Wrap an existing class with a new interface so that it becomes compatible with the client''s expectations.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
// Old Interface
class OldCalculator {
  operations(t1, t2, operation) {
    switch (operation) {
      case ''sum'': return t1 + t2;
      default: return NaN;
    }
  }
}

// New Interface
class NewCalculator {
  add(t1, t2) { return t1 + t2; }
}

// Adapter
class CalcAdapter {
  constructor() {
    this.calc = new OldCalculator();
  }
  
  add(t1, t2) {
    return this.calc.operations(t1, t2, ''sum'');
  }
}
```

---

