  ('design-patterns', 58, 'What is Circuit Breaker?', 'Advanced', 'The Circuit Breaker pattern prevents an application from repeatedly trying to execute an operation that''s likely to fail. It detects failures and encapsulates the logic of preventing a failure from constantly recurring (e.g., during maintenance, temporary external system failure or unexpected system difficulties).', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
The Circuit Breaker pattern prevents an application from repeatedly trying to execute an operation that''s likely to fail. It detects failures and encapsulates the logic of preventing a failure from constantly recurring (e.g., during maintenance, temporary external system failure or unexpected system difficulties).

**Code Example**:
```javascript
if (failures > threshold) openCircuit();
```

