    return sequence & MASK; // Fast bitwise AND instead of expensive modulo (%)
}', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
  ('fintech', 4, 'How do you design a High-Performance Limit Order Book (LOB) matching engine with O(1) order insertion and cancellation?', 'Advanced', 'Represent price levels in a dual structure: 1) A doubly linked list of orders at each price level preserving price-time FIFO priority. 2) A hash map or fixed-size array mapping `order_id` directly to the `Order` node pointer for $O(1)$ cancellation. 3) A sparse price array or AVL/Radix tree of active price levels for $O(1)$ Best-Bid-Offer (BBO) lookup.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
Represent price levels in a dual structure: 1) A doubly linked list of orders at each price level preserving price-time FIFO priority. 2) A hash map or fixed-size array mapping `order_id` directly to the `Order` node pointer for $O(1)$ cancellation. 3) A sparse price array or AVL/Radix tree of active price levels for $O(1)$ Best-Bid-Offer (BBO) lookup.

**Code Example**:
```cpp
struct Order {
    uint64_t order_id;
    uint32_t price;
    uint32_t qty;
    Order* prev;
    Order* next;
};

struct PriceLevel {
    uint32_t price;
    Order* head;
    Order* tail;
};
// order_map[order_id] gives O(1) pointer to directly splice node out on cancel
```

---

