  ('flutter', 5, 'What is the difference between `const` constructors and non-const constructors in Flutter?', 'Beginner', '`const` constructors instantiate widgets at compile-time as canonical singletons. When a parent widget rebuilds, Flutter skips re-evaluating `const` widget subtrees completely, providing significant memory and CPU optimization.', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
`const` constructors instantiate widgets at compile-time as canonical singletons. When a parent widget rebuilds, Flutter skips re-evaluating `const` widget subtrees completely, providing significant memory and CPU optimization.

**Code Example**:
```dart
// Rebuild optimization
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  return Column(
    children: [
      Text(dynamicData),
      const StaticHeaderWidget(), // Never rebuilds!
    ],
  );
}
```

