  ('git', 76, 'How do you recover a lost commit using `reflog`?', 'Advanced', '`git reflog` records updates to the tip of branches. If you accidentally reset --hard or deleted a branch, you can find the commit hash in the reflog and checkout or reset to it.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

