  ('golang', 90, 'How can re-slicing cause memory leaks?', 'Advanced', '**
If you slice a small part of a large array and keep it, the entire underlying array stays in memory. Copy the data to a new slice to release the large array.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
**
If you slice a small part of a large array and keep it, the entire underlying array stays in memory. Copy the data to a new slice to release the large array.

**Code Example**:
```go
var small []byte

func process(large []byte) {
    // Bad: keeps ''large'' in memory
    // small = large[:10]

    // Good: copies only what is needed
    small = make([]byte, 10)
    copy(small, large[:10])
}
```

