  ('html', 6, 'Explain HTML5 Form Validation APIs (`pattern`, `required`, `checkValidity`, `setCustomValidity`)?', 'Beginner', 'HTML5 provides declarative validation constraints (`required`, `pattern`, `min`, `max`, `type="email"`) and JavaScript Constraint Validation APIs (`checkValidity()`, `validity.valid`, `setCustomValidity()`) for localized error messages.', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
HTML5 provides declarative validation constraints (`required`, `pattern`, `min`, `max`, `type="email"`) and JavaScript Constraint Validation APIs (`checkValidity()`, `validity.valid`, `setCustomValidity()`) for localized error messages.

**Code Example**:
```html
<form id="userForm">
  <input id="zip" pattern="[0-9]{5}" required title="5 digit zip code" />
  <button type="submit">Submit</button>
</form>
<script>
const zip = document.getElementById(''zip'');
zip.addEventListener(''input'', () => {
  if (zip.validity.patternMismatch) {
    zip.setCustomValidity(''Please provide exactly 5 digits.'');
  } else {
    zip.setCustomValidity('''');
  }
});
</script>
```

---

