  ('javascript', 42, 'How do you handle errors with `try...catch...finally`?', 'Beginner', '**
Code that might throw an error goes in `try`. Error handling goes in `catch`. Cleanup code (always runs) goes in `finally`.', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
**
Code that might throw an error goes in `try`. Error handling goes in `catch`. Cleanup code (always runs) goes in `finally`.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
try {
  throw new Error("Something went wrong");
} catch (error) {
  console.error(error.message);
} finally {
  console.log("Cleanup operations");
}
```

