  ('javascript', 52, 'What is a Web Worker?', 'Intermediate', '**
Web Workers allow running scripts in background threads. They can perform expensive calculations without blocking the UI thread (main thread). They communicate with the main thread via messages.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
**
Web Workers allow running scripts in background threads. They can perform expensive calculations without blocking the UI thread (main thread). They communicate with the main thread via messages.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
// main.js
const worker = new Worker(''worker.js'');
worker.postMessage(''Start'');
worker.onmessage = (e) => console.log(e.data);

// worker.js
onmessage = (e) => {
  // Heavy computation
  postMessage(''Done'');
};
```

