  ('javascript', 74, 'What is the Singleton Pattern in JS?', 'Intermediate', '**
A design pattern that ensures a class has only one instance and provides a global point of access to it. In JS, object literals are singletons by default, but modules are the modern way.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
**
A design pattern that ensures a class has only one instance and provides a global point of access to it. In JS, object literals are singletons by default, but modules are the modern way.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
// Module Singleton
let instance;
class DB {
  constructor() {
    if (instance) return instance;
    instance = this;
  }
}
export default new DB();
```

---

