  ('javascript', 86, 'What is Shadow DOM?', 'Advanced', '**
It allows you to attach a hidden DOM tree to an element. The shadow DOM is encapsulated, meaning styles inside don''t leak out and global styles don''t leak in.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
**
It allows you to attach a hidden DOM tree to an element. The shadow DOM is encapsulated, meaning styles inside don''t leak out and global styles don''t leak in.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
const host = document.querySelector(''#host'');
const shadow = host.attachShadow({ mode: ''open'' });
shadow.innerHTML = `<style>p { color: red; }</style><p>I am red!</p>`;
```

---

