  ('javascript', 92, 'What is `super` keyword?', 'Beginner', '**
It is used to access and call functions on an object''s parent. In classes, `super()` calls the parent constructor, and `super.method()` calls a parent method.', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
**
It is used to access and call functions on an object''s parent. In classes, `super()` calls the parent constructor, and `super.method()` calls a parent method.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
class Animal {
  constructor(name) { this.name = name; }
}
class Dog extends Animal {
  constructor(name) {
    super(name); // Must call super before accessing ''this''
    this.type = ''dog'';
  }
}
```

---

