  ('microfrontend', 12, 'How do you handle routing in Microfrontends?', 'Advanced', 'The Shell application typically handles the top-level routing (e.g., `/checkout` loads the Checkout MFE). The Microfrontend then handles its own sub-routes (e.g., `/checkout/payment`). Both the Shell and MFEs must listen to the same history object to stay in sync.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
The Shell application typically handles the top-level routing (e.g., `/checkout` loads the Checkout MFE). The Microfrontend then handles its own sub-routes (e.g., `/checkout/payment`). Both the Shell and MFEs must listen to the same history object to stay in sync.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
// Shell: /app1/* -> App1 handles /app1/dashboard
```

