  ('microfrontend', 35, 'What is a Monorepo?', 'Beginner', 'A monorepo stores multiple related projects (shell and all microfrontends) in a single version-controlled repository. This simplifies code sharing, enforces consistent tooling, and makes cross-team refactoring straightforward. The trade-off is that the repository can grow large, so tools like Nx or Turborepo are typically used to manage build caching and avoid rebuilding unaffected projects.', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
A monorepo stores multiple related projects (shell and all microfrontends) in a single version-controlled repository. This simplifies code sharing, enforces consistent tooling, and makes cross-team refactoring straightforward. The trade-off is that the repository can grow large, so tools like Nx or Turborepo are typically used to manage build caching and avoid rebuilding unaffected projects.

