  ('microfrontend', 44, 'What is a Manifest file?', 'Intermediate', 'A manifest file is a JSON configuration that maps each microfrontend name to its deployed URL (or remote entry file). The shell reads this manifest at runtime to discover where to load each MFE from, enabling zero-downtime updates by simply changing the URL in the manifest. A best practice is to serve the manifest from a highly available endpoint and cache it with a short TTL so updates propagate quickly without hammering the server.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
A manifest file is a JSON configuration that maps each microfrontend name to its deployed URL (or remote entry file). The shell reads this manifest at runtime to discover where to load each MFE from, enabling zero-downtime updates by simply changing the URL in the manifest. A best practice is to serve the manifest from a highly available endpoint and cache it with a short TTL so updates propagate quickly without hammering the server.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
{ "app1": "https://cdn.../main.js" }
```

