}', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
  ('nextjs', 4, 'How do Server Actions work in Next.js and how do you handle mutations?', 'Advanced', 'Server Actions (`''use server''`) are asynchronous functions executed on the server, callable directly from forms or client components via standard RPC. They automatically handle POST requests, support progressive enhancement (work without JS), and integrate with `revalidatePath` and `revalidateTag` to update cache.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
Server Actions (`''use server''`) are asynchronous functions executed on the server, callable directly from forms or client components via standard RPC. They automatically handle POST requests, support progressive enhancement (work without JS), and integrate with `revalidatePath` and `revalidateTag` to update cache.

**Code Example**:
```tsx
// app/actions.ts
''use server'';
import { revalidatePath } from ''next/cache'';

export async function updateProfile(formData: FormData) {
  const name = formData.get(''name'') as string;
  await db.user.update({ where: { id: 1 }, data: { name } });
  revalidatePath(''/dashboard/profile'');
}
```

