  registry.example.com/app@sha256:abc...

slsa-verifier verify-artifact app.tar.gz \
  --provenance-path provenance.intoto.jsonl --source-uri github.com/org/repo', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
  ('security', 13, 'What belongs in Security Logging & Monitoring (A09) — and what must NOT?', 'Intermediate', 'Log auth events, access-control denials, input validation failures, and integrity checks with correlation IDs, timestamps (UTC, RFC3339), actor, and resource — shipped to tamper-resistant storage with alerting on anomaly patterns. Never log passwords, tokens, full PII, or card data; redact or hash instead, and document retention.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
Log auth events, access-control denials, input validation failures, and integrity checks with correlation IDs, timestamps (UTC, RFC3339), actor, and resource — shipped to tamper-resistant storage with alerting on anomaly patterns. Never log passwords, tokens, full PII, or card data; redact or hash instead, and document retention.

**Code Example**:
```python
import logging, hashlib
logger = logging.getLogger("audit")

def audit_login(user_id, success, ip):
    logger.info("auth.login", extra={
        "event": "auth.login",
        "actor": hashlib.sha256(user_id.encode()).hexdigest()[:16],  # pseudonymized
        "success": success,
        "ip": ip,
        # NEVER: password, session token, raw email
    })
```

