  ('security', 21, 'How does Clickjacking work and how do you fully prevent it?', 'Beginner', 'An attacker overlays your page in a transparent iframe, tricking users into clicking ("UI redressing"). Modern prevention is CSP `frame-ancestors ''none''` (supersedes the old `X-Frame-Options: DENY`), plus `SameSite` cookies for defense in depth. Sensitive actions should also require user interaction the attacker can''t fake (re-auth, confirmation dialogs).', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
An attacker overlays your page in a transparent iframe, tricking users into clicking ("UI redressing"). Modern prevention is CSP `frame-ancestors ''none''` (supersedes the old `X-Frame-Options: DENY`), plus `SameSite` cookies for defense in depth. Sensitive actions should also require user interaction the attacker can''t fake (re-auth, confirmation dialogs).

**Code Example**:
```javascript
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  res.setHeader("Content-Security-Policy", "frame-ancestors ''none''");
  res.setHeader("X-Frame-Options", "DENY"); // legacy fallback
  next();
});
```

