// name-prefix hardening:
res.cookie("__Host-session", token, { httpOnly: true, secure: true, path: "/" });', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
  ('security', 23, 'What is session fixation and the correct session lifecycle?', 'Intermediate', 'Fixation plants a known session ID (URL, subdomain cookie) before login; the server then attaches the victim''s identity to it. Regenerate the session ID on every privilege change (login, MFA step-up, role switch), accept IDs only from your HttpOnly cookie (never URL), and invalidate server-side on logout with the cookie cleared.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
Fixation plants a known session ID (URL, subdomain cookie) before login; the server then attaches the victim''s identity to it. Regenerate the session ID on every privilege change (login, MFA step-up, role switch), accept IDs only from your HttpOnly cookie (never URL), and invalidate server-side on logout with the cookie cleared.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
app.post("/login", async (req, res) => {
  const user = await authenticate(req.body);
  if (user) {
    req.session.regenerate((err) => {       // NEW id post-authentication
      req.session.userId = user.id;
      res.json({ ok: true });
    });
  }
});
app.post("/logout", (req, res) => {
  req.session.destroy(() => {               // server-side store entry removed
    res.clearCookie("__Host-session");
    res.json({ ok: true });
  });
});
```

---

