  ('security', 43, 'What makes a password-reset token safe?', 'Intermediate', '≥128 bits of CSPRNG entropy, hashed at rest (treat like a password), single-use, TTL ≤15–30min, bound to the requesting account, invalidated on password change and on any new request (or coalesce), delivered out-of-band, and compared in constant time. The flow must re-authenticate (session fixation regeneration) after success.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
≥128 bits of CSPRNG entropy, hashed at rest (treat like a password), single-use, TTL ≤15–30min, bound to the requesting account, invalidated on password change and on any new request (or coalesce), delivered out-of-band, and compared in constant time. The flow must re-authenticate (session fixation regeneration) after success.

