  return url.pathname + url.search;
}', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
  ('security', 61, 'How does path traversal work and what''s the robust defense?', 'Intermediate', 'Inputs like `../../etc/passwd` (or `..%2f`, `....//`, NUL, overlong UTF-8 on Windows) escape the intended directory. Defense-in-depth: reject/normalize with a hardened library, resolve the final path and verify containment (`resolve(base, input).startsWith(base + sep)`), open by validated constructed names only, drop privilege (dedicated user, chroot/container), and never pass user input to file APIs directly.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
Inputs like `../../etc/passwd` (or `..%2f`, `....//`, NUL, overlong UTF-8 on Windows) escape the intended directory. Defense-in-depth: reject/normalize with a hardened library, resolve the final path and verify containment (`resolve(base, input).startsWith(base + sep)`), open by validated constructed names only, drop privilege (dedicated user, chroot/container), and never pass user input to file APIs directly.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
const { resolve, sep } = require("path");
function safeJoin(base, userInput) {
  const target = resolve(base, userInput);
  if (target !== base && !target.startsWith(base + sep)) throw new Error("traversal");
  return target;
}
```

---

