}', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
  ('security', 66, 'What is DOM clobbering?', 'Expert', 'Named DOM elements become global/window properties (`<img name="config">` → `window.config`); injected HTML can clobber variables later used by scripts, turning markup injection into logic manipulation even under CSP. Defenses: sanitize user HTML (DOMPurify with clobbering checks), avoid global lookups on injectable pages, set `id`/`name` allowlists, and use `typeof` guards on sensitive globals.', '**Difficulty**: Expert

**Strategy**:
Named DOM elements become global/window properties (`<img name="config">` → `window.config`); injected HTML can clobber variables later used by scripts, turning markup injection into logic manipulation even under CSP. Defenses: sanitize user HTML (DOMPurify with clobbering checks), avoid global lookups on injectable pages, set `id`/`name` allowlists, and use `typeof` guards on sensitive globals.

**Code Example**:
```html
<!-- injected: -->
<form id="cfg"><input name="isAdmin" value="true"></form>
<script>
  // later code...
  if (window.cfg?.isAdmin) grantAdmin();   // clobbered: form controls, not config
</script>
```

