  ('security', 67, 'How do you secure `postMessage` and WebSocket channels?', 'Advanced', '`postMessage` without `targetOrigin` leaks data to any listening frame; receivers must validate `event.origin` and message shape. WebSockets: enforce `Origin` checks on upgrade, authenticate out-of-band (cookie or first-message token), use `wss://`, validate frame schema/size/rate, and never derive authorization from the client''s claims alone.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
`postMessage` without `targetOrigin` leaks data to any listening frame; receivers must validate `event.origin` and message shape. WebSockets: enforce `Origin` checks on upgrade, authenticate out-of-band (cookie or first-message token), use `wss://`, validate frame schema/size/rate, and never derive authorization from the client''s claims alone.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
// sender
win.postMessage(payload, "https://trusted.example.com");   // never ''*''
// receiver
window.addEventListener("message", (e) => {
  if (e.origin !== "https://trusted.example.com") return;
  if (!messageSchema.test(e.data)) return;
  handle(e.data);
});
```

