  ('security', 69, 'Why does `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` matter?', 'Beginner', 'Browsers MIME-sniff responses and may execute a text/plain file as script — user-controlled content becomes code on your origin. `nosniff` forces the declared Content-Type, closing script-execution and content-confusion vectors (also required for cross-origin read protections). Always pair correct Content-Type with nosniff.', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
Browsers MIME-sniff responses and may execute a text/plain file as script — user-controlled content becomes code on your origin. `nosniff` forces the declared Content-Type, closing script-execution and content-confusion vectors (also required for cross-origin read protections). Always pair correct Content-Type with nosniff.

**Code Example**:
