  ('security', 70, 'What is Subresource Integrity (SRI) and when is it required?', 'Intermediate', 'Third-party `<script>/<link>` tags trust the CDN; a compromised or MITM''d CDN serves malicious code. SRI pins the exact file via `integrity="sha384-..."` — the browser refuses mismatched bytes. Required for cross-origin static assets; combine with `crossorigin="anonymous"` for CORS caching. Useless for frequently-changing files — pin versions instead of `latest`.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
Third-party `<script>/<link>` tags trust the CDN; a compromised or MITM''d CDN serves malicious code. SRI pins the exact file via `integrity="sha384-..."` — the browser refuses mismatched bytes. Required for cross-origin static assets; combine with `crossorigin="anonymous"` for CORS caching. Useless for frequently-changing files — pin versions instead of `latest`.

**Code Example**:
```html
<script src="https://cdn.example.com/purify@3.0.6/purify.min.js"
        integrity="sha384-<base64-sha384>"
        crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
```

