  ('security', 79, 'How do you verify incoming webhooks (Stripe/GitHub-style)?', 'Intermediate', 'Webhook URLs are secret-weak; verify a signature over timestamp+payload: constant-time HMAC check against the registered endpoint secret, reject stale timestamps (±5min) to blunt replay, respond 2xx fast, and process async via a durable queue with idempotent handlers — senders retry aggressively.', '**Difficulty**: Intermediate

**Strategy**:
Webhook URLs are secret-weak; verify a signature over timestamp+payload: constant-time HMAC check against the registered endpoint secret, reject stale timestamps (±5min) to blunt replay, respond 2xx fast, and process async via a durable queue with idempotent handlers — senders retry aggressively.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
app.post("/webhooks/stripe", express.raw({ type: "application/json" }), (req, res) => {
  const sig = req.header("stripe-signature");   // t=...,v1=...
  const event = stripe.webhooks.constructEvent(req.body, sig, process.env.STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET);
  queue.add("stripe-event", event);             // async processing
  res.sendStatus(200);
});
```

