  ('security', 92, 'What belongs in a security code-review checklist?', 'Beginner', 'Authn on every route; authz server-side per resource (never client-enforced); input validation at trust boundaries with schema; output encoding per context; secrets absent (scan); rate limits on sensitive endpoints; safe defaults (deny, secure cookies); error handling without stack traces; and dependencies pinned with scan evidence. If any row fails, block merge — consistency beats heroics.', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
Authn on every route; authz server-side per resource (never client-enforced); input validation at trust boundaries with schema; output encoding per context; secrets absent (scan); rate limits on sensitive endpoints; safe defaults (deny, secure cookies); error handling without stack traces; and dependencies pinned with scan evidence. If any row fails, block merge — consistency beats heroics.

