  let totalComponents = 0;
</script>
```

---

<a id="q31"></a>', '<script context="module">
  let totalComponents = 0;
</script>', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
  ('svelte', 31, 'How do you handle fallback content in slots?', 'Beginner', 'Fallback content in slots provides sensible defaults for reusable components when the consumer does not supply custom content. Any markup placed inside a `<slot>` tag is rendered only when the parent omits that slot, making components work out of the box while remaining extensible. A common pitfall is assuming fallback content is always rendered alongside consumer content, but it is completely replaced when content is provided.', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
Fallback content in slots provides sensible defaults for reusable components when the consumer does not supply custom content. Any markup placed inside a `<slot>` tag is rendered only when the parent omits that slot, making components work out of the box while remaining extensible. A common pitfall is assuming fallback content is always rendered alongside consumer content, but it is completely replaced when content is provided.

**Code Example**:
```javascript
<slot>Default Content</slot>
```

---

<a id="q32"></a>', '<slot>Default Content</slot>', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
  ('svelte', 32, 'What is `$$props`?', 'Advanced', 'An object containing all props passed to the component. Not recommended for general use.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
An object containing all props passed to the component. Not recommended for general use.

