  ('system-design', 124, 'What is Write Amplification?', 'Expert', '**
When one logical write results in multiple physical writes to storage (e.g., during LSM compaction or B-Tree page splitting). Reduces SSD lifespan and throughput.', '**Difficulty**: Expert

**Strategy**:
**
When one logical write results in multiple physical writes to storage (e.g., during LSM compaction or B-Tree page splitting). Reduces SSD lifespan and throughput.

**Code Example**:
```text
Write 1KB data -> Triggers merge -> Rewrites 10MB file.
Amplification = 10MB / 1KB.
```

