  ('typescript', 74, 'When is `@ts-ignore` acceptable versus `@ts-expect-error`?', 'Beginner', '`@ts-expect-error` fails when the suppressed error disappears — self-cleaning, so it''s the only acceptable suppression for known limitations. `@ts-ignore` silently rots. Neither should paper over genuine bugs; prefer guards or `unknown` handling, and lint-count all suppressions.', '**Difficulty**: Beginner

**Strategy**:
`@ts-expect-error` fails when the suppressed error disappears — self-cleaning, so it''s the only acceptable suppression for known limitations. `@ts-ignore` silently rots. Neither should paper over genuine bugs; prefer guards or `unknown` handling, and lint-count all suppressions.

**Code Example**:
```typescript
