  ('vue', 7, 'How does `<Suspense>` handle async components in Vue 3?', 'Advanced', '`<Suspense>` orchestrates loading states for nested async dependencies (components with `async setup()` or top-level `await`), displaying a `#fallback` template until all async components resolve.', '**Difficulty**: Advanced

**Strategy**:
`<Suspense>` orchestrates loading states for nested async dependencies (components with `async setup()` or top-level `await`), displaying a `#fallback` template until all async components resolve.

**Code Example**:
```vue
<template>
  <Suspense>
    <template #default>
      <AsyncUserProfile :userId="userId" />
    </template>
    <template #fallback>
      <div class="skeleton-loader">Loading profile...</div>
    </template>
  </Suspense>
</template>
```

